WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.950
Moving house.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:13.950
A cup of tea?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.950
Yes dear.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.950
Ah.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.950
Yeah, Stuart.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.950
Here you are.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.950
Yes dear.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Oh.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.950
I'll go and open the door for Boris, Josie.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.950
Why do I have to do it?

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Don't argue. Just do it.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.950
Get down Boris.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:42.950
Here you are Boris.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:43.950
Have my piece of toast.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.950
Don't feed him at the table, Josie.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.950
There's another competition in the newspaper I can enter Nancy.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.950
What can you win this time?

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.950
A ticket for a Marilyn Manson concert.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.950
Do you know who that is?

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.950
No, but isn't she a singer? A bit like Nanamoo Scory.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.950
Yes, that's right. Just like her. I hope you win.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.950
Oh, just ignore him mum.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.950
Nancy, it says here that your day is going to be full of fun and laughter.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.950
I don't think so.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.950
Why do you look at the horoscope every day mum?

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.950
It's fun. Let me look at Josephine's stars.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.950
Oh yes, here it is.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:34.950
It says that you're feeling off colour today and it's better to stay indoors.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.950
Yeah, you're right, Grand. I have a stomach ache.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.950
I'm not going to school today.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.950
Stop that Josephine. You are going to school. No arguments.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.950
Oh, why do I have to go to school? I hate it. It's boring.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:48.950
Because you do.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.950
I hated school too.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.950
The teachers were terrible. They used to cane us with sticks.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.950
Oh, do they cane you, Grand?

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.950
Yes, of course. I was cained by the headmaster.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:06.950
What was his name? Oh yes, Mr. Payne. I put some glue on a seat.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.950
That's not so bad. Why did he cane you?

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.950
Because it was the teacher's toilet seat.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.950
Really? Wow.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.950
Don't get ideas, Josephine. Go and get ready for school.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.950
Mom, please.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.950
Do as I tell you now.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.950
Teenagers.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.950
And put that newspaper down, Pete.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.950
Sorry? Is there a problem?

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.950
No, no.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:40.950
I was just trying to get our daughter to go to school.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.950
Thank you for helping me.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.950
It's OK, dear. I'm always happy to help.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.950
Can you pass the toast, please?

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.950
Didn't you hear what I said?

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.950
Yes, dear, of course, dear. And the tree core, please.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.950
Here it is.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.950
Ow! Why did you do that? Look, it's all over my trousers.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.950
I don't believe it. Get down, Boris.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.950
I'm not playing. To something.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.950
Go to work now, Pete, before I do something else to you.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.950
The next time, it might be a kitchen knife, so be careful in future.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.950
What's the matter? What did I do?

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.950
Nothing, Pete. Absolutely nothing. That's the problem.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.000
I'm going. Good-bye.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.950
Why did you marry him, Nancy?

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.950
Do you want someone you as well?

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.950
I always said he was bone idle.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.950
I liked that lawyer you went out with once. Nice eyes and a lovely smile.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.950
Do you hear what you think, Mum?

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.950
Ooh! It's not a good day for Pete.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:53.950
It says in his horoscope that he gets some bad news this afternoon.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.950
Stop it, Mum. Don't make things worse.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.000
I must tell Pete. He must be careful.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:04.950
Nancy.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.950
Yes? What do you want now?

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.950
I can't find any clean trousers.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.950
They're in the fridge between the cheese and the tomatoes.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.950
Why are they in the fridge?

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.950
Where do you think they are? In the bedroom.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:22.950
Left wardrobe on the right, where they always are.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:23.950
Thank you, Nancy.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.950
Pete. Yes? What do you want?

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.950
Be careful. Today is a bad day for you.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:30.950
Sorry?

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.950
It says in your horoscope that you get some bad news.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.000
Not that rubbish again. I'm not interested.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.950
Wait a minute.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.950
Do you believe all that rubbish in the horoscope?

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.950
Sometimes it's true, you know.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.950
Well, you're the same star sign as me, so you be careful.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.950
Ooh dear, I forgot.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.950
Maybe you fall down the stairs.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.950
Maybe Boris bites your leg.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.950
Maybe your hearing aid explodes.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:57.950
Maybe.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:58.950
Goodbye.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.950
I'll find it.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.000
They dirty deed.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.950
I told you not to say anything.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.950
Now, where is Josephine? She's going to be late.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.950
Can you go upstairs and tell us a hurry up, please, Mum?

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.950
I have to make her sandwiches.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.950
Oh, what a family.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.950
OK, Nancy.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.950
Come on, Boris.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:26.950
There's a good dog.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:30.000
You don't want to bite my leg, do you?

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.950
Oh, there you are, Josie.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.950
Come on, your mother is waiting.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.950
Josh, close the door, Grand.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.950
Can you keep a secret?

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.950
Oh, I love secrets.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.950
Come here.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.950
Look here.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.950
In this box.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:00.950
Oh, it's Robbie the Rat.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:01.950
I thought...

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:02.950
Yes, we know.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:03.950
Dad told me to sell him.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.950
But I want to keep him.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.950
Oh, he's so sweet.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:12.950
Oh, look at his lovely little eyes and funny nose.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.950
He really looks like your father.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:19.950
Don't tell Mum or Daddy's here in my room.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:20.950
Please?

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:21.950
I promise.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.000
It's our secret.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:35.950
It's nice to put my feet up for a moment.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.950
You work too hard.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:41.950
Pete and Josephine should do more around the house to help you.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.950
Stop it, Mum.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.950
Can you pass me another biscuit, please?

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:52.000
I just want a few minutes of peace and quiet.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:54.950
Oh, dear.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.950
I wonder who that is.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.950
Can you answer it, Mum?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.950
All right.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.950
Hello?

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.950
Who is it?

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:06.950
Sorry.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:08.950
Pete.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:09.950
Speak up.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:10.950
What does he want?

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.950
Sorry?

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:13.950
Yes.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:14.950
All right.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:15.950
Bye.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:16.950
Yes?

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.950
He said he's coming home now.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:20.950
But what did he want?

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.950
Something about he forgot the bag.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.950
What are you talking about, Mother?

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.950
It was a terrible line.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.950
All I could hear was the sound of cars.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.950
I think he was phoning with his mobile.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.950
His what?

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:35.950
It's, er...

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.950
Oh, it doesn't matter.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.950
I want to know why he's coming home.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:43.950
It's only two o'clock in the afternoon.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:46.950
I told you today was going to be a bad day.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.950
I can feel it in my bones.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.950
I wonder what happened at work.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:54.950
It must be serious, don't worry.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:56.950
He just forgot something, I think.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.950
Yes, you're right.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:07:59.950
Okay.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.950
I can't sit around anymore.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.950
I can make Josephine's bed and tidy her room.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.000
Thanks, Mum.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:12.950
Can you change the sheets, please?

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:15.000
Yes, Nancy.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:23.000
Now, where are you, you little thing?

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.950
Oh, there you are.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.950
Oh, you're so sweet and cute.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.950
Come here.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:34.000
Oh, it tickles.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.950
Stop it, Boris.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.950
Here, Robbie.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:41.950
Don't be afraid.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.950
What's that, Mum?

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:44.950
Nothing.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.000
Nothing.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.950
Oh, don't do that.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:49.950
Come out.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.950
Oh, that tickles.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.950
How are you?

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.950
Oh, come out of my jumper.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:58.000
Oh, no, stop that.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.950
What's happening in here?

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.950
Oh, no, stop that.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:06.950
Oh, get off, Boris.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:08.950
Oh, bad.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.950
What's the matter with everyone in this house?

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.950
Who are you talking to, Mum?

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.950
Oh, that tickles, stop it.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:15.950
What's happening?

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:16.950
I'm home.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:18.950
What's the noise?

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:19.950
Oh, hello, Pete.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.000
I'm coming.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:24.950
Is that your mother?

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:25.950
Yes.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.950
I don't know what she's doing.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.950
Maybe she'll head Sherry on her cornflakes.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.950
She's a Josephine's room, laughing her head off, and I don't know why.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.000
Boris is sitting looking at her.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.950
She's getting old, Nancy.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:43.950
Maybe we should start looking for an old fossils home for her.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:44.950
Oh, don't start that again.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.950
You know I get angry.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:52.950
Mum is staying with us, and they are called old people's homes, not old fossils homes.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:54.950
Well, I think we seriously...

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:56.950
We can talk about this another time.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:58.950
Why are you home so early?

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:00.950
You've never come home at this time.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.950
Oh, yes.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.950
Look, can we go into the kitchen?

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.000
I can't concentrate with a laughing hyena upstairs.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.950
Sit down, dear.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.950
Would you like a cup of tea?

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.950
Something stronger might be a better idea.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:19.950
Why?

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:20.950
What happened this morning?

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.950
Tell me, please.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.950
I lost my job.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:25.950
What?

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:26.950
Yes.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:27.950
I lost my job.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:29.950
I am now unemployed.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.950
Six of us from the office got the sack.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:37.000
We can work until the end of the month, and then thank you, but goodbye.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.950
But I don't understand.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:43.950
Oh, that's what you were trying to tell mum on the phone.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:46.950
She thought you said you forgot the bag.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.950
She's deaf as well as losing her marbles.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:50.950
Beat.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.950
OK, OK.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:58.950
Well, as I was saying, the company needs to save money, and my department is being closed.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:00.950
What are we going to do?

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:02.950
I can find another job.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:03.950
I hope.

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.950
I think we must move house, though.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:08.950
This one is too big and too expensive.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:10.950
We must save money.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:11.950
Wait a minute.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:13.950
I need to think.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.950
Be quiet, mother.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:19.000
I'm just going to shut my mother up.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:23.000
I'm just going to shut my mother up.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.950
What is the matter with you?

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.950
Calm down, please.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:36.950
Stop it.

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.950
Calm down and come downstairs.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:41.950
Peter's lost his job.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:42.950
Oh, no.

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:44.950
I knew today it was a bad day.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.000
Why are you laughing?

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:49.950
Yes, you are.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:50.950
No, I'm not.

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:52.950
It's terrible.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:54.950
Oh, this is impossible.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.000
Stay there.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.950
Here you are, Boris.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:16.000
There might be the last time you have meat for your dinner.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.950
What are we going to do, Boris?

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.950
I wonder what we're going to do.

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:25.950
I'm home.

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:27.950
I'm hungry.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:30.950
School is bloody boring.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.950
Teachers are so dumb.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:34.950
I don't know anything.

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:35.950
I'm starving.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:36.950
I want some crisps.

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:39.950
If you wait five minutes, Josie, you can have something cooked.

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:40.950
I'm making a curry.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:42.950
No, crisps are great.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:46.000
I want to find Julia.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:48.950
She was at school all day today with you.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:49.950
Can't she wait?

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:50.950
I want to talk to you.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:51.950
See ya.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.000
But Jo?

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:58.000
It's easier to have a conversation with you, Boris.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:12:59.950
Boris?

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.950
Boris?

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:04.000
Come back, Boris.

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:06.950
When is dinner?

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:07.950
In five minutes.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:08.950
Okay.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:10.950
I just need to finish some repairs on the car.

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:11.950
That can wait.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.950
There are more important things to talk about.

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:15.950
Like what?

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:18.950
What planet do you live on, Pete?

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.950
At the end of the month, you have no job.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:22.950
Oh, yes.

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:23.950
I forgot.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:24.950
You forgot?

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:26.950
Don't you think we need to talk about it?

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:28.950
I suppose so.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.950
Where do we move to?

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:34.950
What do we say to Josie and Mum?

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:36.950
I went to the estate agent some way home.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:41.950
I got some information about a really nice two bedroom flat in Cedar Road near the park.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.950
Why didn't you ask me to come?

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:45.950
I am your wife, you know.

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:48.950
When we sell the house, we can easily buy this flat.

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:51.950
It's got a nice balcony and a small garden.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.950
You know you are always saying that the garden here is too big.

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:55.950
There's too much cleaning and...

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:57.950
Yes, yes, I know.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:59.950
We can go and look at the flat this evening.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.000
Okay.

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:02.950
Wait a minute.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:05.950
How many bedrooms did you say the flat has?

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:06.950
Back in a minute.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:08.950
You've got to do something in the garage.

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:11.950
Did you say two bedrooms?

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:12.950
But...

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.950
Where does my mother sleep?

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:15.950
Ooh.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.950
I feel a little strange.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.950
My muscles ache from so much laughing.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.950
Still don't understand why you were laughing.

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:27.950
I think I need a little sherry to calm my nerves.

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:28.950
Back in a minute.

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:30.950
What a house.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.950
It's like a railway station.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:33.950
I'm so hungry.

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:34.950
I want some biscuits.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.950
Just sit down, Josephine.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:38.950
You can have some biscuits in a minute.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:40.950
Pete?

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:41.950
Mom?

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.950
Come in the kitchen.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:45.950
Now!

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:48.950
I said now!

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:50.950
Keep your hair on, Mom.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:51.950
Chill out.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:54.950
How can I chill out when your father's lost his job today?

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:55.950
What?

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:56.950
Yes.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:57.950
You heard me.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:59.950
We have to move soon.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:00.950
Find a smaller house.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:01.950
I want my own room.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:02.950
Yes, of course.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.950
I'm not sharing with anyone.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.950
Oh, that's better.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:07.950
A little sherry.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:08.950
It always helps.

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:09.950
Can you sit down?

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:11.950
Please, Mother.

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:13.950
Perhaps you need a sherry too?

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:15.950
No, I don't.

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:17.950
What's the problem, Nancy?

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:20.950
Can we all sit down together?

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.950
Good.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.950
Right.

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:26.950
Listen.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:30.950
In a few weeks, Pete has no job.

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:32.950
We have to move.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.950
Oh, what a terrible day.

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:37.950
And you bad things were going to happen.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:38.950
Be quiet, Mother.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:39.950
Please.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:42.950
Yes, and I know the perfect place for us.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:44.950
It's in Cedar Road next to the park.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:46.950
I'm very close to your school, Josie.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.950
And the city centre.

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:49.950
It's perfect.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:52.950
My friend, Julia, is just around the corner.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:53.950
Great.

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:55.950
Cedar Road is near the Bingo Club.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:57.950
I can walk there.

00:15:58.000 --> 00:15:59.950
I don't need to get a taxi.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:00.950
I don't like taxis.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:01.950
Tax is always smelly.

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:02.950
Yes.

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:03.950
Okay, Mom.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:07.950
But the problem is that the flat Pete found has only got.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:10.950
And Boris can walk in the park.

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:17.950
As I was saying, the flat Pete found for us only five minutes to walk to the shops.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.950
It only has two bedrooms.

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.950
Oh, no.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:26.950
I don't want to go into an old people's home.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.950
They're full of old people.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:29.950
Don't worry, Mom.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.950
You don't have to go into a home.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.950
There isn't any other alternative.

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:35.950
Yes, there is.

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:37.950
I'm sure we can find another solution.

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:40.950
Sorry, but you're going to have to go into the home.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:41.950
That's life.

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:43.950
It's all right.

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:45.950
I know you don't want me here.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:51.950
Last week, John, my friend at Bingo, said I can go and live with him.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:56.950
He needs someone to help him, as he can't see very well.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:57.950
He's blind.

00:16:58.000 --> 00:16:59.950
Good thing too.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.950
Are you sure you want to do that, Mom?

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.950
It's a great idea, Nancy.

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.950
Yes, I'm very sure.

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.950
You and Josie can visit me any time.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:10.950
It is nearby.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:11.950
There we are.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:13.950
Everyone is happy.

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:15.950
Pass a biscuit, Josie.

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:16.950
Thanks.

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:18.950
Can't sit here doing nothing.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:22.950
Daddy is horrible to you, Grand.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:24.950
Why doesn't he like you?

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:26.950
A good question, Josie.

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:29.950
Does he like anyone on the planet?

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.000
Only himself.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:40.000
Wake up, Pete.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:42.950
What?

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:45.950
Well, not now, Naomi.

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.950
Oh, it's you, Nancy.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.950
Yes, it's Nancy.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:51.950
Your wife, remember?

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.950
Yes, of course, Nancy.

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:55.950
Why did you wake me up?

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:57.950
Because...

00:17:58.000 --> 00:17:59.950
Who's Naomi?

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:00.950
Who?

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:02.950
What do you mean, who's Naomi?

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.950
You said not now, Naomi, when I woke you up.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:06.950
I'm sure I didn't.

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:07.950
You did it.

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.950
Where did you think I was?

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:12.950
I was dreaming of Naomi Campbell.

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:14.950
Are you sure?

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:17.950
If not, we can talk about this later.

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:19.950
Come on, get out of bed.

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:21.950
It's Saturday.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:24.000
I always get up late.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.950
It's only half past nine.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:27.950
Don't argue.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:28.950
Get up.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:29.950
It's Mum.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.950
What?

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.950
Did you pop a clog in the night?

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:34.950
No, I'm pleased to say.

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:36.950
Come on, hurry up.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:38.950
I'm going downstairs.

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:40.950
They want all of us.

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:41.950
What do you mean?

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:43.950
They want all of us.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:47.950
I suppose I have to get up.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:50.950
Can you wait until tonight, Naomi?

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:52.950
I'm coming, I'm coming!

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:54.950
Just waiting in the kitchen, Mum.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:56.950
Josie, Pete's on his way.

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:58.950
This is so exciting.

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:00.950
I think I need to go to the toilet.

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:02.950
Do they want me in the photograph as well?

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:04.950
Yes, the whole family.

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:05.950
And Boris.

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:06.950
And Robbie.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:07.950
Oh.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:08.950
Robbie?

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:11.950
Your father told you to sell that rat.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:12.950
Oh.

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:13.950
Well.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:14.950
No.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.950
I forgot to tell you, Mum.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:19.950
I forgot to tell you.

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:21.950
Don't worry.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:24.950
You know he's very quiet and clean and he can stay in my room.

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:26.950
But I told you to.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:27.950
But his house trained.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:28.950
He's so nice.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:30.950
Yes, I know.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:33.950
He is quite sweet, but what about your father?

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:36.950
I'm sure you can think of something to say to him.

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:38.950
Please don't tell him.

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:41.950
I have to think of something to say to him.

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:42.950
Children.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:43.950
What a life.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:44.950
Okay.

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:46.950
Just keep quiet.

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:47.950
Leave it to me.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:48.950
Thanks, Mum.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:51.950
What are the strange people in our living room on a Saturday morning?

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.950
You still have your pajamas on?

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:54.950
Yes.

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:57.950
I didn't expect to find my house full of people.

00:19:58.000 --> 00:19:58.950
What's happening?

00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:00.950
Oh, mega embarrassing.

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:03.950
Why are you wearing those pajamas on?

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:04.950
I don't know.

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:05.950
I don't know.

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:06.950
I don't know.

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:07.950
I don't know.

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:08.950
I don't know.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:09.950
I don't know.

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:10.950
I don't know.

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:11.950
I don't know.

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:12.950
I don't know.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.950
Why are you wearing those pajamas?

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:15.950
I bought them.

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:16.950
What's wrong with them?

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:18.950
I like Winnie the Pooh.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:20.950
Ticker is my favourite.

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:21.950
He's always so good.

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:23.950
Can we all stop discussing my pajamas?

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:25.950
There's nothing about tickeries.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:26.950
Be quiet.

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:29.950
What's the matter with everyone this morning?

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.950
Why are they sitting on our lounge?

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:32.950
Because of Mum.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:33.950
What did she do?

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:35.950
Win the Nobel Prize for physics.

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:36.950
No, Pete.

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:39.950
She's our new special envoy at the United Nations.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:41.950
Don't we say nasty, Pete?

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:42.950
No.

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:45.950
Mum won a competition at Tesco's.

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.950
A year supply of baked beans.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:49.950
No, something much more exciting.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:50.950
A lifetime supply.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:51.950
A toilet paper.

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:53.950
No, Pete.

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:56.950
Mum won a house.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:57.950
A house?

00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:59.950
A house?

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.950
A what?

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:02.950
For Boris?

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:03.950
No.

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:06.950
You do know what a house is, don't you?

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:08.950
Of course I do, but...

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:09.950
I don't understand.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:13.950
Mum entered a competition at the supermarket last month.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:18.950
She had to guess how many jars of Marmite was sold in Britain every week.

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:23.950
The prize for the nearest guess was a new detached house.

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:24.950
She won it.

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:25.950
I won it.

00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:26.950
I won it.

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:33.950
I had no idea what the answer was, so I wrote down the first number that came into my head.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:36.950
63,360.

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:39.950
I remember it from my primary school days.

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:41.950
Amazing.

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:43.950
Absolutely amazing.

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:46.950
Why 63,360 grand?

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:49.950
It's the number of inches in a mile.

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:51.950
Amazing.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:53.950
Absolutely amazing.

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:55.950
Your cool grand.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:56.950
Awesome.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:58.950
And the people in our lounge?

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:03.950
It's the local photographer from the newspaper and someone from the supermarket.

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:07.950
They want to take our photo and give us the key to the house.

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:09.950
Does this mean we can all live together?

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:11.950
We don't have to move into a flat.

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:13.950
Yes, that's right.

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:16.950
Is that all right with you, Pete?

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:18.950
Yes, I suppose so.

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:19.950
Awesome.

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:20.950
Come on, let's go.

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:21.950
I'm coming.

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:25.950
It is my hair all right, Josie.

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:29.950
We're one big happy family again.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:33.950
I'm so happy we can go on living with your mother.

00:22:34.000 --> 00:22:36.950
We must be very grateful to her.

00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:39.000
That's the problem.

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:54.950
It's a lovely house, Pete.

00:22:55.000 --> 00:22:56.950
I went to look at it this morning.

00:22:57.000 --> 00:22:59.950
It's ready and we can move in when we want.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:02.950
It's more modern than this house.

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:04.950
The bathroom's a wonderful.

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:06.950
The kitchen is wonderful.

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:08.950
Everything is wonderful.

00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:10.950
The garden is wonderful.

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:12.950
Yes, yes, I get the picture.

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:14.950
Can you organise a removal firm?

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.950
There are lots of advertisements in the yellow pages.

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:18.950
Leave it to me.

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:20.950
I have a friend at work who knows a firm.

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:21.950
I hope they're good.

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:22.950
Yes, yes.

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:23.950
Don't worry.

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:26.950
You are happy to move into this house with Mum, aren't you, Pete?

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:27.950
Yes, dear.

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:32.950
I mean, we have to move because of your job and this is the best alternative.

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:33.950
Yes, dear.

00:23:34.000 --> 00:23:35.950
I know you're right.

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:38.950
And this house is looking so shabby.

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:40.950
What do you mean?

00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:41.950
Let's start.

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:43.950
Just look at this wallpaper here in the dining room.

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:44.950
I like it.

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:46.950
No, you don't.

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:48.950
It's 23 years old.

00:23:49.000 --> 00:23:50.950
You just don't like doing DIY.

00:23:51.000 --> 00:23:52.950
I don't mind DIY.

00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:55.950
When was the last time you did anything in this house?

00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:56.950
Um...

00:23:57.000 --> 00:23:58.950
Can you see?

00:23:59.000 --> 00:23:59.950
I'm right.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:00.950
No, wait.

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:03.950
I changed the light bulb in the kitchen last month.

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:05.950
Need I say any more?

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:07.950
Anyway, can we stop arguing?

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:08.950
We're not arguing.

00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:09.950
Yes, we are.

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:10.950
No, wait.

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:11.950
This is stupid.

00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:12.950
I agree.

00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:13.950
Come on.

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:16.950
We said we wanted to start for sorting out today.

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:17.950
Okay.

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:20.950
We can start with this cupboard of stuff.

00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:22.950
Do you never use any of it?

00:24:23.000 --> 00:24:23.950
Look, these for a start.

00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:24.950
No.

00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:25.950
Don't throw them out.

00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:26.950
Why not?

00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:27.950
They are old.

00:24:28.000 --> 00:24:28.950
We never use them.

00:24:29.000 --> 00:24:30.950
They might be useful one day.

00:24:31.000 --> 00:24:32.950
What use are six?

00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:33.950
Six?

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:34.950
Salt and pepper pot.

00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:37.950
Perhaps we have visitors in the new house.

00:24:38.000 --> 00:24:38.950
Visitors?

00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:40.950
How many are you expecting?

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:43.950
The entire Hampshire cricket team and their wives.

00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:44.950
And the crowd.

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:46.950
There's no need to be like that, Pete.

00:24:47.000 --> 00:24:49.950
I just don't like to throw things away.

00:24:50.000 --> 00:24:52.950
But we said we were going to throw things out.

00:24:53.000 --> 00:24:55.950
We have too much stuff and we don't need it all in the new house.

00:24:56.000 --> 00:24:56.950
I know.

00:24:57.000 --> 00:24:58.950
But it's so difficult.

00:24:59.000 --> 00:25:00.950
What have we put in the box for the car boot sale?

00:25:01.000 --> 00:25:02.000
Let me look.

00:25:05.000 --> 00:25:05.950
A broken egg cup.

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:08.950
Two tea towels from Mallorca.

00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:12.000
A frying pan with no handle and...

00:25:13.000 --> 00:25:13.950
Aah!

00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:15.950
Cuckoo clock with only one hand.

00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:17.950
Not very impressive for three hours work, is it?

00:25:18.000 --> 00:25:18.950
No, it isn't.

00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:19.950
Okay.

00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:22.950
We must try to be more ruthless.

00:25:23.000 --> 00:25:24.950
What do you mean we?

00:25:25.000 --> 00:25:25.950
Yes, I know.

00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:26.950
All right, Pete.

00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:27.950
Good.

00:25:28.000 --> 00:25:29.950
Now what is this?

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:31.950
A back of the cupboard.

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:32.950
Give it to me.

00:25:33.000 --> 00:25:36.950
It's still in its original box.

00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:39.950
It can't be important, surely.

00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:42.950
It's a pasta machine for making fresh pasta.

00:25:43.000 --> 00:25:46.950
You don't like pasta, so it can definitely go to the car boot sale.

00:25:47.000 --> 00:25:48.950
But wait a minute, Pete.

00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:50.950
Now we don't need it.

00:25:51.000 --> 00:25:54.950
I just want to look at it for a moment.

00:25:55.000 --> 00:25:56.950
Okay now?

00:25:57.000 --> 00:25:57.950
Yes.

00:25:58.000 --> 00:25:58.950
You're right.

00:25:59.000 --> 00:26:00.950
We don't need it.

00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:02.950
Into the car boot box.

00:26:03.000 --> 00:26:05.950
Might get five pounds for that.

00:26:06.000 --> 00:26:08.950
You know it was a wedding present, Pete.

00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:09.950
Really?

00:26:10.000 --> 00:26:13.950
Another useless present, a complete waste of money.

00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:16.000
The things people buy.

00:26:17.000 --> 00:26:19.950
Why didn't we write a wedding list for everyone to choose from?

00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:22.950
Because you said it's more fun to see what people buy us.

00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:23.950
Did I?

00:26:24.000 --> 00:26:24.950
I don't remember.

00:26:25.000 --> 00:26:26.950
Anyway, into the car boot box.

00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:29.950
What a load of rubbish.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:32.950
You know that it was a present from your parents.

00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:33.950
What?

00:26:34.000 --> 00:26:35.950
The pasta machine.

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:36.950
Are you sure?

00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:37.950
Yes.

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:39.950
Look closely at the side of the box.

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:41.950
You can see they wrote their names.

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:42.950
Let me look.

00:26:43.000 --> 00:26:44.950
You're right.

00:26:45.000 --> 00:26:47.950
We can't throw this out, can we?

00:26:48.000 --> 00:26:50.950
Might be useful one day, Nancy.

00:26:51.000 --> 00:26:51.950
But you said...

00:26:52.000 --> 00:26:53.950
No, it's from my parents, dear.

00:26:54.000 --> 00:26:54.950
Right.

00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:55.950
What's next?

00:26:56.000 --> 00:26:58.950
What's in these drawers?

00:26:59.000 --> 00:27:02.950
Interesting.

00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:04.950
I didn't know you were a member of Appa.

00:27:05.000 --> 00:27:06.950
Are you talking about...

00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:08.950
Oh, this photo.

00:27:09.000 --> 00:27:10.950
What are you wearing?

00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:11.950
It was fashionable then.

00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:13.950
Everyone was wearing those skirts.

00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:15.950
What did you do with it?

00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:17.950
I would love to see you in it now.

00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:19.950
Don't get up stairs.

00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:21.950
Let me go and look.

00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:22.950
It's okay.

00:27:23.000 --> 00:27:25.000
I was only joking.

00:27:27.000 --> 00:27:28.950
What do you think, Boris?

00:27:29.000 --> 00:27:32.950
Prepare yourself for a shock, Nancy, in a mini skirt.

00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:35.950
I must try not to laugh too much.

00:27:36.000 --> 00:27:38.950
You keep quiet too, Boris.

00:27:39.000 --> 00:27:40.950
Here she comes.

00:27:41.000 --> 00:27:42.950
Now remember, Boris, don't start laughing.

00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:44.950
Here I am.

00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:46.950
What do you think?

00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:50.950
I think it shrunk in the wardrobe.

00:27:51.000 --> 00:27:52.950
Well?

00:27:53.000 --> 00:27:56.950
Well, say something.

00:27:57.000 --> 00:27:58.950
It's...

00:27:59.000 --> 00:28:00.950
It's...

00:28:01.000 --> 00:28:02.950
So you think it's funny, do you?

00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:04.950
No, it's...

00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:05.950
It's...

00:28:06.000 --> 00:28:06.950
It's...

00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:08.950
It's interesting, dear.

00:28:09.000 --> 00:28:10.950
Is that all you can say?

00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:12.950
No, no, no. It's...

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:14.950
Interesting and...

00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:17.950
Very interesting, dear.

00:28:18.000 --> 00:28:19.950
I want to keep it on.

00:28:20.000 --> 00:28:21.950
It reminds me of Happy Days.

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:23.950
Yes, you do that, dear.

00:28:24.000 --> 00:28:28.950
I need to go outside to wash the flowers.

00:28:29.000 --> 00:28:29.950
No.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:30.950
What's the car?

00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:31.950
No.

00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:34.000
Back in a minute, dear.

00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:42.950
We're moving at the weekend, Pete.

00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:44.950
Please come and help me.

00:28:45.000 --> 00:28:45.950
Where are you?

00:28:46.000 --> 00:28:47.950
I'm in the loft.

00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:50.950
There are so many boxes here.

00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:52.950
What's in them?

00:28:53.000 --> 00:28:53.950
Which boxes?

00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:55.950
Oh, those are my things.

00:28:56.000 --> 00:28:56.950
Don't throw them out.

00:28:57.000 --> 00:28:58.950
They're old things for my school days.

00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:00.950
I want to look at them.

00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:01.950
Oh, do we really have to?

00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:03.950
I want to look at them.

00:29:04.000 --> 00:29:06.950
See if you were a good pupil at school.

00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:08.950
Okay, here you are.

00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:10.950
What's this?

00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:13.950
Oh, how sweet.

00:29:14.000 --> 00:29:16.950
It's your first writing book from primary school.

00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:18.950
It's embarrassing, Nancy.

00:29:19.000 --> 00:29:19.950
No, it's sweet.

00:29:20.000 --> 00:29:21.950
Look what you wrote.

00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:23.950
My name is Peter.

00:29:24.000 --> 00:29:24.950
I have a mother.

00:29:25.000 --> 00:29:25.950
She cooks.

00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:27.950
I have a father.

00:29:28.000 --> 00:29:30.000
He sleeps on the sofa.

00:29:31.000 --> 00:29:32.950
Yes, he did.

00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:33.950
And look here.

00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:36.950
There's a picture of you in a swimming costume.

00:29:37.000 --> 00:29:37.950
How sexy.

00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:39.950
No, I look terrible.

00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:42.950
I think that was the first time we went to blackpool.

00:29:43.000 --> 00:29:45.950
I was six years old.

00:29:46.000 --> 00:29:47.950
What's this?

00:29:48.000 --> 00:29:49.950
I don't believe it.

00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:51.950
It's my old school uniform.

00:29:52.000 --> 00:29:52.950
On an awful colour.

00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:54.950
Did I really have to wear that to school?

00:29:55.000 --> 00:29:58.950
Oh, dark blue and pink stripes is very fashionable these days.

00:29:59.000 --> 00:29:59.950
Please, try it on.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:01.950
I want to see what it looks like.

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:02.950
No, I'm not.

00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:03.950
It's too small.

00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:04.950
Oh, please.

00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:05.950
Just for me.

00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:06.950
Come on.

00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:07.950
I can help you.

00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:08.950
I don't want to.

00:30:09.000 --> 00:30:09.950
Oh, don't be so stupid.

00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:10.950
Come on.

00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:11.950
No!

00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:12.950
Get off, Nancy!

00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:13.950
Ah!

00:30:14.000 --> 00:30:14.950
Oh!

00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:15.950
Oh!

00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:16.950
Oh!

00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:17.950
My leg!

00:30:18.000 --> 00:30:18.950
Where am I?

00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:19.950
Oh!

00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:20.950
Oh, no!

00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:22.950
There's a toddler in my room.

00:30:23.000 --> 00:30:24.950
He's coming through my ceiling.

00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:25.950
No!

00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:26.950
Oh!

00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:27.950
My leg!

00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:28.950
Oh!

00:30:29.000 --> 00:30:29.950
Oh!

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:30.950
Oh!

00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:31.950
Oh!

00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:33.950
Stop it, you stupid!

00:30:34.000 --> 00:30:34.950
Stop it!

00:30:35.000 --> 00:30:35.950
Stop it!

00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:36.950
Stop it!

00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:37.950
It's Pete!

00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:38.950
Oh!

00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:40.950
Don't worry, he's not dangerous.

00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:42.950
Just stupid.

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:45.950
Is that you, Pete?

00:30:46.000 --> 00:30:46.950
Yes it is.

00:30:47.000 --> 00:30:47.950
Who else do you think it is?

00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:49.950
My foot hurts.

00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:52.950
Why is your foot through my ceiling?

00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:54.950
You know I have a weak heart.

00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:56.950
I almost died of fright.

00:30:57.000 --> 00:30:59.950
I always put my foot through the ceiling.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:01.950
It's a hobby of mine.

00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:02.950
What?

00:31:03.000 --> 00:31:04.950
What did you hit it with?

00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:06.950
I thought you were a burglar.

00:31:07.000 --> 00:31:08.950
I hit it with a bedside lamp.

00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:10.950
I think it's broken.

00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:11.950
I don't care about your lamp.

00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:13.950
I think my foot is broken.

00:31:14.000 --> 00:31:15.950
Help me, Nancy.

00:31:16.000 --> 00:31:16.950
Oh!

00:31:17.000 --> 00:31:17.950
Be careful!

00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:18.950
Oh!

00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:19.950
Don't be stupid.

00:31:20.000 --> 00:31:20.950
You can stand up.

00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:21.950
Come on.

00:31:22.000 --> 00:31:22.950
I can't.

00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:24.950
You just want some sympathy.

00:31:25.000 --> 00:31:25.950
I can't stand up.

00:31:26.000 --> 00:31:26.950
Oh!

00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:27.950
Oh!

00:31:28.000 --> 00:31:28.950
Oh!

00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:29.950
Oh!

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:31.950
Perhaps you can't stand.

00:31:32.000 --> 00:31:33.950
Come on, Pete.

00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:35.950
Put your arm around my shoulder.

00:31:36.000 --> 00:31:37.950
Let me carry you to the bed.

00:31:38.000 --> 00:31:38.950
Oh, my God.

00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:39.950
Don't be so silly.

00:31:40.000 --> 00:31:40.950
Let me look.

00:31:41.000 --> 00:31:41.950
Oh.

00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:43.950
Oh, it's only sprained.

00:31:44.000 --> 00:31:45.950
There are lots of bruises.

00:31:46.000 --> 00:31:48.950
That's because your mother hit it with her lamp.

00:31:49.000 --> 00:31:49.950
She's very brave.

00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:50.950
Brave?

00:31:51.000 --> 00:31:52.950
She's dangerous.

00:31:53.000 --> 00:31:54.950
Send her away to any war zone.

00:31:55.000 --> 00:31:56.950
She could sort it out.

00:31:57.000 --> 00:31:58.950
Britain's answer to Mambo.

00:31:59.000 --> 00:32:00.950
She is 72 years old.

00:32:01.000 --> 00:32:01.950
Hey, Mambo.

00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:04.950
How about a week in the Middle East if they need your help?

00:32:05.000 --> 00:32:06.950
I think you're suffering from shock.

00:32:07.000 --> 00:32:07.950
Oh.

00:32:08.000 --> 00:32:08.950
Here's some aspirin.

00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:09.950
Try to rest for a few hours.

00:32:10.000 --> 00:32:12.950
I can finish looking in the boxes in the attic.

00:32:13.000 --> 00:32:13.950
I can help.

00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:15.950
Oh, it's okay.

00:32:16.000 --> 00:32:17.950
I want to...

00:32:18.000 --> 00:32:19.950
Oh.

00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:20.950
Oh.

00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:21.950
Oh.

00:32:22.000 --> 00:32:37.950
The

00:32:38.000 --> 00:32:39.950
removal van is here.

00:32:40.000 --> 00:32:40.950
Okay.

00:32:41.000 --> 00:32:41.950
Is everything ready?

00:32:42.000 --> 00:32:42.950
Where's Pete?

00:32:43.000 --> 00:32:43.950
I'm ready.

00:32:44.000 --> 00:32:46.950
Oh, this is so exciting.

00:32:47.000 --> 00:32:49.950
Our new house and our new life.

00:32:50.000 --> 00:32:52.000
Where's Pete?

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:00.950
Good morning.

00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:01.950
Come in.

00:33:02.000 --> 00:33:02.950
Good morning.

00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:03.950
Thank you.

00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:04.950
Come on, Jim.

00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:06.000
In we go.

00:33:07.000 --> 00:33:08.950
There are only two of you.

00:33:09.000 --> 00:33:09.950
Is that enough?

00:33:10.000 --> 00:33:11.950
Jim and I always work together.

00:33:12.000 --> 00:33:13.950
No problem, madam.

00:33:14.000 --> 00:33:16.950
He may be over 65, but he can carry us over.

00:33:17.000 --> 00:33:18.950
No problem.

00:33:19.000 --> 00:33:20.950
Where do you want to start?

00:33:21.000 --> 00:33:23.950
Maybe a cup of tea before we start.

00:33:24.000 --> 00:33:26.950
It's a long day and we're both thirsty.

00:33:27.000 --> 00:33:29.950
Er, yes, I suppose that's all right.

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:31.950
Come into the kitchen.

00:33:32.000 --> 00:33:34.950
Perhaps you have a packet of biscuits as well.

00:33:35.000 --> 00:33:37.950
A bit of toast and marmalade would be very nice.

00:33:38.000 --> 00:33:39.950
All right.

00:33:40.000 --> 00:33:41.950
Sit down if you can find a chair.

00:33:42.000 --> 00:33:44.950
Everything is packed and ready for the move.

00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:45.950
We're okay.

00:33:46.000 --> 00:33:47.950
Don't worry about us.

00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:49.950
Oh, my back.

00:33:50.000 --> 00:33:52.950
Bit of a problem with my back, but it's okay.

00:33:53.000 --> 00:33:55.950
No problem, no problem.

00:33:56.000 --> 00:33:58.950
I'm in the living room if you want me.

00:33:59.000 --> 00:33:59.950
Don't worry.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:01.950
We can start in a few minutes.

00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:03.950
Come here, doggy.

00:34:04.000 --> 00:34:06.000
Would you like a biscuit?

00:34:14.000 --> 00:34:14.950
Where's Pete?

00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:16.950
Why didn't you organise a proper removal company?

00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:19.950
The two of them are sitting in the kitchen eating breakfast.

00:34:20.000 --> 00:34:21.950
I think they were the cheapest.

00:34:22.000 --> 00:34:24.950
Why didn't I organise it myself?

00:34:25.000 --> 00:34:27.950
I can't get Pete to do anything.

00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:29.950
Where is he?

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:30.950
Pete!

00:34:31.000 --> 00:34:32.950
Oh, I must go and find him.

00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:33.950
You stay here, mother.

00:34:34.000 --> 00:34:36.000
Okay, Nancy.

00:34:40.000 --> 00:34:40.950
Here I am.

00:34:41.000 --> 00:34:41.950
What is happening?

00:34:42.000 --> 00:34:43.950
Good morning, sir.

00:34:44.000 --> 00:34:44.950
Nice dog.

00:34:45.000 --> 00:34:45.950
Hello, Pete.

00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:49.950
But why are you all sitting here eating?

00:34:50.000 --> 00:34:51.950
Don't feed Boris, please.

00:34:52.000 --> 00:34:53.950
I know, George.

00:34:54.000 --> 00:34:55.950
Is it my bingo club?

00:34:56.000 --> 00:34:58.950
We have a great time together, don't we, George?

00:34:59.000 --> 00:35:01.950
We certainly do, dear.

00:35:02.000 --> 00:35:04.950
Something happened to your legs, sir.

00:35:05.000 --> 00:35:05.950
It doesn't look good.

00:35:06.000 --> 00:35:06.950
Don't ask.

00:35:07.000 --> 00:35:08.950
But that's not important at the moment.

00:35:09.000 --> 00:35:12.950
I paid a lot of money to have you move us to our new house.

00:35:13.000 --> 00:35:15.950
I did not pay for you to eat our food.

00:35:16.000 --> 00:35:19.950
And stop giving Boris my favourite biscuits.

00:35:20.000 --> 00:35:21.950
Don't be so unfriendly.

00:35:22.000 --> 00:35:23.950
I am not unfriendly.

00:35:24.000 --> 00:35:26.950
I just want these men to start work.

00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:27.950
Okay.

00:35:28.000 --> 00:35:29.950
We understand.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:32.000
Come on, Jim.

00:35:38.000 --> 00:35:38.950
Oh.

00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:39.950
There you are.

00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:41.950
